lee.json: LEE Filters colour range

The names and the CIE x, y values in lee.json are LEE Filters' published tungsten
(3200 K) chromaticity data, taken from https://leefilters.com (page of each filter
under /colour/). (c) Panavision / LEE Filters. They are used with LEE Filters'
permission, given by email on 2026-11-17: LEE Filters support wrote that we are
welcome to use the publicly available information on leefilters.com.

The data remain LEE Filters'. Diffusion, neutral-density and polariser filters are
left out.

The file was made by fetch-lee.py in this folder (python3 -I fetch-lee.py), which
read leefilters.com on 2026-11-17.
